<Base title="Appearing in the District of New Jersey">
  <div class="breadcrumb" slot="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &nbsp;›&nbsp; Appearing in D.N.J.</div>

  <div class="pagehead">
    <h1>Appearing From Outside New Jersey</h1>
    <div class="role">Admission, association, and how cases are assigned</div>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Pro hac vice</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Counsel admitted elsewhere may appear in this district pro hac vice under L. Civ. R.
        101.1(c). The rule requires association with a member of the bar of this court who signs the
        pleadings and remains responsible in the matter.
      </p>
      <p>
        This page states the rule and argues nothing. Read the rule and the judge's own standing
        orders before relying on either.
      </p>
      <div class="footlinks">
        <a href="https://www.njd.uscourts.gov/court-info/local-rules-and-orders" rel="noopener">Local rules and orders</a>
        <a href="https://www.njd.uscourts.gov/standing-orders" rel="noopener">Standing orders</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Vicinages</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The district sits in Camden, Newark and Trenton. Case assignment follows the court's
        published vicinage lines rather than the convenience of counsel.
      </p>
      <div class="footlinks">
        <a href="https://www.njd.uscourts.gov/vicinage-lines-case-assignment" rel="noopener">Vicinage lines and case assignment (court)</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
